test Command and [ ]

The test command is used to check conditions.

You will commonly see:
[ condition ]

For eg,
if [ -f /etc/passwd ]; then
    echo "File exists"
fi

Here -f means regular file exists.

Common file tests

| Test | Meaning                      |
| ---- | ---------------------------- |
| `-f` | File exists                  |
| `-d` | Directory exists             |
| `-e` | File or directory exists     |
| `-r` | File is readable             |
| `-w` | File is writable             |
| `-x` | File is executable           |
| `-s` | File exists and is not empty |

Eg:
#!/bin/bash

FILE="/etc/passwd"

if [ -f "$FILE" ]; then
    echo "$FILE exists"
else
    echo "$FILE does not exist"
fi

Eg:
DIR="/backup"

if [ -d "$DIR" ]; then
    echo "Backup directory exists"
else
    echo "Backup directory does not exist"
fi
